A particle used in the following senses:--
.²1 Named, called, by name; {#himAlayo nAma nagADirAjaH#} <ls>Ku. 1. 1</ls>; {#tannandinIM#}
 {#suvfttAM nAma#} <ls>Dk. 7</ls>.
.²2 Indeed, certainly, truly, forsooth, verily, to be sure; {#mayA nAma#}
 {#jitam#} <ls>V. 2. 17</ls>; {#vinItavezeRa pravezwavyAni tapovanAni nAma#} <ls>Ś. 1</ls>;
 {#ASvAsitasya mama nAma#} <ls>V. 5. 16</ls> ‘when I was just consoled’; {#tannAma#}
 {#nizWurAH puruzAH#} <ls>Mk. 5. 32</ls> ‘that means men are cruel’.
.²3 Probably, perhaps; <ab>oft.</ab> with {#mA#}; {#aye padaSabda iva mA nAma rakziRaH#}
 <ls>Mk. 3</ls> ‘perhaps (but I hope not) that of guards’; {#mA nAma akAryaM kuryAt#} <ls>Mk. 4</ls>.
.²4 possibility; {#tavEva nAmAstragatiH#} <ls>Ku. 3. 19</ls>; {#tvayA nAma munirvimAnyaH#}
 <ls>Ś. 5. 20</ls> ‘is it possible <ab>&c.</ab>’ (implying censure); frequently used with
 {#api#} in the sense of ‘I wish’, ‘would that’, ‘is it likely that <ab>&c.</ab>’;
 see under {#api#}.
.²5 A feigned or pretended action, pretence ({#alIka#}); {#kArntAntiko#}
 {#nAma BUtvA#} <ls>Dk. 130</ls>; so {#BIto nAmAvaplutya#} <ls n="Dk.">104</ls> ‘as if afraid’, {#pariSramaM#}
 {#nAma vinIya ca kzaRam#} <ls>Ku. 5. 32</ls>.
.²6 (With imperatives) Granted, though, it may be, well, it may be; {#tad#}
 {#Bavatu nAma SokAvegAya#} <ls>K. 328</ls>; {#atanuzu viBavezu jYAtayaH santu nAma#}
 <ls>Ś. 5. 8</ls>; <ls>Bh. 1. 16</ls>; {#evaM nAmAstu#} ‘be it so, if you like’; {#karotu#}
 {#nAma nItijYo vyavasAyamitastataH#} <ls>H. 2. 14</ls> ‘though he may exert himself’; <ls>Māl. 10. 7</ls>.
.²7 Anger or censure; {#mamApi nAma daSAnanasya parEH pariBavaH#} <ls>G. M.</ls>;

 (the sentence may imply ‘censure’ also); {#kiM nAma visPuranti SastrARi#}
 <ls>U. 4</ls>; {#mamApi nAma sattvEraBiBUyante gfhAH#} <ls>Ś. 6</ls>.
.²8 Wonder; {#AScaryamanDo nAma putraM drakzyati#} <ls>Sk.</ls>
.²9 Recollection. {#nAma#} is often used with the interrogative pronoun
 and its derivatives {#kaTam, kadA#} <ab>&c.</ab> in the sense of ‘possibly’, ‘indeed’,
 ‘I should like to know’; {#ayi kaTaM nAmEtat#} <ls>U. 6</ls>; <ls>R. 16. 82</ls>; <ls>Bh. 2. 44</ls>;
 <ls>H. 1. 104</ls>; {#ko nAma rAjYAM priyaH#} <ls>Pt. 1. 146</ls>; {#ko nAma pAkABimuKasya#}
 {#janturdvArARi dEvasya piDAtumIzwe#} <ls>U. 7. 4</ls>.
